# ECS Component Guidelines

## Component Structure

All components must extend `ECS.Component`:

```typescript
import * as ECS from '../../../libs/pixi-ecs';

export class MyComponent extends ECS.Component {
  // Properties
  private myProperty: number = 0;

  constructor() {
    super();
    // Set fixed frequency if needed
    // this.fixedFrequency = 60;
  }

  onInit() {
    // Initialize once, subscribe to messages
    this.subscribe('MY_MESSAGE');
  }

  onUpdate(delta: number, absolute: number) {
    // Update every frame
  }

  onMessage(msg: ECS.Message) {
    // Handle messages
  }
}
```

## Component Best Practices

### DO:
- Keep components focused (single responsibility)
- Use messages for cross-component communication
- Use `fixedFrequency` for game logic (not frame-dependent)
- Subscribe to messages in `onInit()`
- Clean up in `onRemove()` if needed

### DON'T:
- Don't store references to other components
- Don't update other objects directly (use messages)
- Don't make components too large (split into multiple)
- Don't use components as data containers (use attributes)

## Component Communication

**Always use messages for communication:**

```typescript
// Sender
this.sendMessage('PLAYER_DIED', { cause: 'enemy' });

// Receiver
onInit() {
  this.subscribe('PLAYER_DIED');
}

onMessage(msg: ECS.Message) {
  if (msg.action === 'PLAYER_DIED') {
    // Handle death
  }
}
```

## Fixed Timestep

For consistent game logic, use `fixedFrequency`:

```typescript
constructor() {
  super();
  this.fixedFrequency = 60; // Update at 60 Hz
}

onFixedUpdate(delta: number, absolute: number) {
  // Consistent behavior regardless of frame rate
}
```
